why gabby would make the  worst imposter in among us  instead of playing it cool and showing  sympathy for the orphans who lost their  parents to titans  she says they haven't accepted their  guilt over the atrocities the people of  the island have committed  she says even if kaya acts like a saint  her sins are too great and  that's why her parents died this is how  messed up  and brainwashed gabby is she blames  innocent people for the tragedies that  happened in their lives  just because of what their ancestors  supposedly did  before they even arrive to this island  and kaya straight up asks  if that's what marlei teaches them this  is a great turn  and we're just lucky gabby didn't kill  her because she did try to  luckily falco interfered and saved kaya  kaya has all the reasons  in the world to call for help and admit  who these guys are  but she actually tells the others that  gabby just got jealous  because she thinks that kaia is stealing  her brother meaning falco  another hilarious moment that came out  of a very scary situation  where gabby almost killed another  innocent person  however kaia is building their trust at  this point since she helped them and  revealed she knew their secret but  didn't rat them out  she continues to help them she even goes  to a secluded place with them  which is just kind of crazy to me but  hey kaya is fearless now apparently kaia  talks about the girl meaning sasha who  saved her from a titan  she first watched as her mother was  being eaten alive  still probably one of the most creepy  and terrifying scenes  in all of attack on titan kaia can't  understand why the island aldians are  hated so much that people would actually  put them through something like this  gabby says it's because her kind  slaughtered people for thousands of  years but that applies to herself just  as much as tukaya the fact is kai and  her mother were born on the island  and had nothing to do with the eldians  who mistreated other cultures and people  i liked this conversation a lot and i  think hayah does a great job of showing  gabby that her logic doesn't make any  sense kaya actually gets more fired up  than gabby  during this exchange talking about her  mother's death and how she did nothing  wrong to deserve it  gabby is pretty much arguing probably  based on marlene teachings that eldians  must be punished for the sin of their  ancestors while kaya  is arguing that humans should be judged  on their own lives  and i think it's clear that kaya makes  way more sense the son shouldn't be  punished for the sins of the father  and he definitely shouldn't be punished  for the sins of his great great  grandfather what matters is what you do  with the life you're given  we aren't born into the world lesser or  more deserving of punishment than anyone  else  and that's what i think gabby is  starting to get although the  brainwashing has  clearly got quite the grip on her psyche  it's finally falco who apologizes saying  kaya's mother did nothing wrong  sometimes bad things happen to good  people it doesn't mean they deserved it  and here kaia says he doesn't need to  apologize  because he was just born in marley he's  not responsible for the actions of that  nation  just as kaya wants them to recognize her  as a human being not as a dehumanized  member of the enemy side  she is ready to return the favor despite  all the terrible things gabby says and  does  kaia still wants to help them and  invites them to a marlene restaurant  where they might be able to find a way  back home  and it's interesting to see how sasha  continues to live on even after her  death  in the form of kaya and everyone else  whose life she helped shape  what we do in life has ripple effects on  those around us  and even though sasha is dead her  willingness to risk her life and save  kaya led to kaya not only surviving but  becoming the kind of person who wants to  help others  it's crazy to think that sasha was  killed by gabby and that now kaya who  was saved by sasha  is helping gabby see that the ldns here  can be good and kind people  gabby has the girl she killed to thank  for her starting to break  through the mental chains that still  weigh her down this part  clearly shows that barriers can be  overcome with the help of kindness  bravery  empathy and time but people may die  before those barriers drop  that's the tragic part as is the fact  that they may take really long to drop  if they do at all we also get a part  near the end where marlei has realized  that zeke faked his death and they were  thinking about waiting six months to  attack with their allies but reiner is  like  he advises an immediate surprise attack  so we may see more action sooner than  expected for the preview it's called  guides  and we're asked who should one hate who  should one blame and there's mention of  a shifting truth  i love that term shifting truth and you  definitely get a lot of shifting truths  as you go through attack on titan in  this preview we also see a huge  explosion so there will definitely be  action the next episode but this one was  really good too  we didn't have titan fights but we had  important philosophical questions posed  and discussed  like whether we're born free and pure or  whether we're born  chained to the past needing to atone for  the sins of our ancestors there was  extremely important stuff about gabby  who it's easy to hate but we gotta keep  in mind she is brainwashed  af and she treats island aldian so  horribly in part because she is so  uncomfortable with her own status  as a devil aka as an aldian this in no  way makes her actions okay but it helps  explain why she acts the way she does  and i really think  kaya is helping her question her  ingrained biases  and long-held assumptions and how is she  doing this by simply being a good and  kind person to  her kaya is lucky that falco is there  though or she might have been dead  before she could show gabby  that not all island aldians are devils  but anyways that is it for this episode  review  let me know what you thought of it and  what you expect to see happening next i  loved seeing how sasha's actions during  her life continued to influence people  to this day who in turn influence others  and the world  so even if we aren't immortal this  reminds us that our actions and  treatment of others today  can have ripple effects into eternity a  powerful thought that i absolutely love  if you do enjoy seeing these attack on  time videos and want to keep them coming  then the best thing you could do is  warhammer smash that like button and  share this video with any attack on  titan fans that you know  if you haven't be sure to subscribe and  this is crucial hit that notification  bell and select  all or you will miss future attack on  titan videos and while you wait for the  next insane episode to drop  feel free to check out our growing  attack on time playlist where we got  videos about all the time shifters and  their powers all the acronyms and their  powers the titans rank for weak is the  strongest and much more  link to that is in the description you  can also check out our anime version  podcast where we discuss  anime with people who haven't seen them  before and we are currently talking  about attack on titan so check it out  you can relive the amazing series with  us  link to that is in the description as  well and i especially want to thank the  patron squad over on patreon and here on  youtube who helped make videos like this  one possible first and foremost i want  to thank  the patron of legend the one  acknowledged by lord tuigo himself  and the most donated champion of the  world alpha sigma  and are the one tier patrons the ones  who stand atop all clans  in grotto the world acquire respect but  they have a liam thompson  al-jatal dr cortman johnny boy draws  emperor taku  spidey life tinel baked buddhist and  tungsten tarkis and are pro hero to your  patrons the 